/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  CaHPO4 DI-CAFOS A60, LUBRICATED (formulation F 0-100) -- out-of-die solid fraction, in-die strain and diametral
  strength at six compaction pressures; Kukuls & Mohylyuk, RSU Dataverse
  (2025), doi:10.48510/FK2/MFMNDR, CC BY 4.0, file `F_0-100.tab`.

  The formulation (2.0 % sodium stearyl fumarate, 0.3 % colloidal silica)
  and the protocol (STYL'One Nano, 11.28 mm flat punches, 70 rpm, 500 mg)
  are those of Mohylyuk et al., Pharmaceutics 16 (2024) 362 (CC BY).  Every
  value is the MEAN of ten tablets as the file prints it.
    P        computed HERE: the upper-punch peak force of the MAIN
             compression (the file's second `Upper punch peak force` row; the
             first is the 5 kN pre-compression) over the punch face
             pi (11.28 mm)^2 / 4 = 99.93 mm2.  The file prints no pressure.
    D        `Solid fraction (%)` / 100 -- OUT OF DIE (measured after
             ejection), on the true density the file's ReadMe states.
    C        (H0 - h)/H0 with H0 the `Filling height` and h the main
             compression's `Compression thickness` -- IN DIE.
    F, d, t  `Hardness (N)`, `Diameter (mm)`, `Thickness (mm)`.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
provenance
{
    source         "Kukuls, K., Mohylyuk, V., Direct compression of lubricated mixture of microcrystalline cellulose and calcium phosphate dibasic anhydrous, RSU Dataverse (2025), doi:10.48510/FK2/MFMNDR";
    licence        "CC BY 4.0 (dataset record)";
    transcribed    "from F_0-100.tab of the dataset, read 2026-11-02";
    reviewStatus   interim;
}

columns
(
    { name P; unit MPa; }      // main-compression pressure (upper punch)
    { name D; unit -; }      // out-of-die solid fraction
    { name C; unit -; }      // in-die Kawakita strain
    { name F; unit N; }      // hardness (diametral breaking force)
    { name d; unit mm; }      // diameter
    { name t; unit mm; }      // out-of-die thickness
);

data
(
       95.464  0.6538  0.25937     14.4   11.29   2.68
      142.296  0.6901  0.29683     24.7   11.30   2.54
      243.163  0.7370  0.34006     49.1   11.30   2.39
      338.327  0.7660  0.36599     73.7   11.31   2.30
      435.693  0.7928  0.38617     98.9   11.31   2.22
      478.722  0.7814  0.39481    111.1   11.31   2.24
);
